Ours (dsv41 recipe), Apache-2.0, against vLLM main 6e517b15 + patches 0001-0008 + 0010.
DSpark Markov bias rows cached for frequent tokens (VLLM_DSPARK_MARKOV_CACHE=<json token list>,
VLLM_DSPARK_MARKOV_CACHE_ROWS, default 4096). V4.1's Markov bias depends only on the previous token
(markov_w2 @ markov_w1[t]), and the full-vocab path reads the whole replicated 129,280 x 256 BF16 markov_w2 (66 MB) at
every draft position (5 x 262 us = 1.38 ms a step at DSpark 5 on GB10). The rows of the listed tokens are computed at
load and read back (258 KB a row); cached and computed rows come from the same Triton kernel, so a token's bias has the
same bits either way. Same idea as TensorFold's V4.1 drafter (github.com/bertholomus/TensorFold, branch
deepseek-v41-tp2, families/deepseek_v41/cuda/markov.py, Apache-2.0: 4096 rows); our implementation. Token list:
data/dspark/markov_top_tokens.json (most frequent first, counted on our calibration set: top 4096 cover 79.7% of its
tokens). Drafts can differ from the cuBLAS path's only where its rounding differs (acceptance noise, verification
unchanged). Test: patches/tests/test_dspark_markov_cache.py.

